{
  "name": "497. An output folder belongs to the virtual key that first writes there, with what lies inside it (storage folder ownership) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-7121. Local fixture regression, no live provider call: run with providerErrorFixture=1 against the gateway of tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json, with tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs as the only upstream. A provider writes a batch's result files beneath the output folder the request named, with the operator's shared credential. Those files have no ownership rows, so before TXE-7121 any virtual key that learned their names could read them, and a second key could write its own batch into the same folder. Now a virtual key that names an output location claims it as a folder before the provider is called. The claim needs an exclusive location: no folder of another key at or above it, and nothing recorded for another key beneath it. A stored object in a folder claimed by another key is not found. The provider is the OpenAI-shaped stand-in storage_uri_files (the fixture's /pp/storage); what the folder pins is the gateway's check, which runs before any provider call and is the same code for every provider. The folder names carry a per-run suffix because a claim outlives the key that made it. 497.1 and 497.2 create two keys. 497.3 is key A's first batch into a/out. 497.4 to 497.9 are key B: a result file in that folder as an input, the same file by its https URL, a batch into the same folder, into a folder inside it, into the folder that holds it, and a video task writing there, each 404 before any provider call. 497.10 is key B writing into a sibling folder. 497.11 and 497.12 are key A reading and writing in its own folder. 497.13 is a folder that only shares a name prefix. 497.14 is key A refused inside key B's folder. 497.15 reads the fixture's wire log: only the served requests reached the provider.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "497.1 [setup] virtual key A (writes first)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "  return;",
              "}",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('folderVkA'); pm.collectionVariables.unset('folderVkAId');",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__reset', method: 'POST' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('the fixture was reset', function () { pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null); pm.expect(res.code).to.equal(200); });",
              "});",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('folderRun', String(Date.now()) + '-' + Math.floor(Math.random() * 1000000));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the virtual key was created', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.equal(200); });",
              "var created = (pm.response.json() || {}).virtual_key || {};",
              "pm.test('it has an id and a value', function () { pm.expect(created.id, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); pm.expect(created.value, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); });",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('folderVkA', created.value || ''); pm.collectionVariables.set('folderVkAId', created.id || '');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"name\": \"harness-497-a-{{$guid}}\", \"provider_configs\": [{\"provider\": \"storage_uri_files\", \"weight\": 1, \"allowed_models\": [\"*\"], \"key_ids\": [\"*\"]}]}",
          "options": {
